# Move one hand to a point, planned by MoveIt against the planning scene from where the arm is
# now: for pointing at something and for gestures a learned skill makes. The arm must be acquired.
# "left" or "right".
string arm
# Where, in any frame TF knows; the server transforms it into its planning frame.
geometry_msgs/PointStamped target
# Added to the target in the planning frame's axes, which are the robot's (x forward, y left,
# z up), m.
geometry_msgs/Vector3 offset
# "reach" takes the hand to the target plus the offset. "point" puts it on the line from the
# shoulder to that point, the server's pointing reach from the shoulder, so the arm points at it;
# where that line leaves the hand in front of the torso, it steps out to its own side.
string mode
# A fraction of the server's speed for these moves, above 0 and at most 1; 0 takes the whole.
float64 speed
---
bool success
string message
---
